\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Real part of the field of values $W(X)$ and $\|I-X\|_2$ for $X=\tilde  A_{R}\mathcal  S$, $\tilde  A_{R}E$, $\tilde  A_{R}\mathcal  M$ (exact coarse solves, the Pauli--Villars factor regularized), $m=0.001$, with the multigrid of the mass scan (16 low modes, 32 test vectors, $4^4$, Chebyshev of Table~\ref {tab:setups}) but no levels below the coarse lattice. Rows ``4 configs.'' and ``no smearing'': ranges over the four $12^4$ configurations ($M_5=1$ without smearing); other rows configuration~1. On $24^4$ only $W(\tilde  A_{R})$ is given (Krylov dimensions 10 and 12 agree to six digits); there the field of values of $\tilde  A_{R}\mathcal  M$ did not settle (the two dimensions differ by $2\%$) and the eigensolvers did not fit in $24$\,GB of device memory.}}{38}{table.14}\protected@file@percent }
